==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la|en}} {{term|patricia||noble|lang=la}}; later also seen as the feminine form of the saint's name [[Patrick]].

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{given name|female|}}.

====Usage notes====
The name was formerly rare in English, but became popular in the 20th century, partly due to a Princess Patricia (1886-1974), a granddaughter of Queen Victoria, so named since she was born on St. Patrick's day.

